From 1056eb9ab54d357a307e995eefa846f4f234d1f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:55:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-media: an empty CAPTURE queue is not POLLERR

poll() raised EPOLLERR whenever the CAPTURE queue had no queued buffer
and no pending DQBUF. POLLERR lands in revents regardless of the
requested mask, so v4l2_codec2's V4L2DevicePoller returned from every
poll() immediately and re-polled: measured on the board (RPi4 DomA,
1080p60 H.264, 11 CAPTURE buffers) POLL = 6551/s against DQBUF = 140/s
and QBUF = 76/s, i.e. 47 polls per dequeue.

vb2_core_poll() raises EPOLLERR only for !streaming, q->error and
q->waiting_for_buffers, and the OUTPUT branch of this same function was
corrected the same way in "virtio-media: EPOLLOUT means dequeueable,
not has a free slot". This driver tracks neither q->error nor
waiting_for_buffers, so a streaming CAPTURE queue that has had no QBUF
since REQBUFS or STREAMOFF, which vb2 also reports as EPOLLERR, polls
as not ready here.

Blocking is safe for the only consumer we have: v4l2_codec2's
V4L2Device::poll() calls ::poll() with timeout -1 and keeps an
interrupt fd in the set, so it is woken either by a completed buffer or
by its own wakeup pipe.

Change-Id: I775f978b77f70d8032f7a66fbfa0e7cd9599a691
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 driver/virtio_media_driver.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/driver/virtio_media_driver.c b/driver/virtio_media_driver.c
index 050f099..0c3a873 100644
--- a/driver/virtio_media_driver.c
+++ b/driver/virtio_media_driver.c
@@ -826,9 +826,22 @@ static __poll_t virtio_media_device_poll(struct file *file, poll_table *wait)
 
 	mutex_lock(&session->queues_lock);
 	if (req_events & (EPOLLIN | EPOLLRDNORM)) {
-		if (!capture_queue->streaming ||
-		    (capture_queue->queued_bufs == 0 &&
-		     list_empty(&capture_queue->pending_dqbufs)))
+		/*
+		 * Only a queue that is not streaming is an error. An empty
+		 * CAPTURE queue is not: POLLERR is reported in revents
+		 * whether or not the caller asked for it, so raising it just
+		 * because no buffer is queued yet turns every poll() into a
+		 * busy loop. Measured on RPi4 DomA 2026-09-05 with 11 CAPTURE
+		 * buffers and 1080p60 H.264: POLL 6551/s against DQBUF 140/s
+		 * (47 polls per dequeue). vb2_core_poll() raises EPOLLERR only
+		 * for !streaming, q->error and q->waiting_for_buffers; this
+		 * driver tracks neither of the last two, so a streaming queue
+		 * with nothing to dequeue simply polls as not ready, as the
+		 * OUTPUT branch below does. v4l2_codec2's V4L2Device::poll()
+		 * passes timeout -1 and also watches an interrupt fd, so
+		 * blocking here is what it wants.
+		 */
+		if (!capture_queue->streaming)
 			rc |= EPOLLERR;
 		else if (!list_empty(&capture_queue->pending_dqbufs))
 			rc |= EPOLLIN | EPOLLRDNORM;
